What is Maven ? 
         Maven is a build automation & dependency management tool mainly used for Java projects.
         In simple words, Maven downloads libraries, builds code, runs tests, and creates deployable files (JAR/WAR) automatically.
         It is maintained by Apache Maven.

Why Do We Even Need Maven?
Imagine this situation 
  You wrote a Java application
       It needs external libraries (Spring, Log4j, etc.)
  You must:
       Compile code
       Run tests
       Create a JAR/WAR file
       Share the build with others
Doing all this manually is time Conusming and there will be an human Error 
          " Maven automates all of this " 

Before Maven :
    Developers manually downloaded JAR files
    Different versions on different machines
    No standard project structure
    Builds failed on other systems

With Maven :
    Automatic dependency download
    Same build everywhere
    Standard folder structure
    Easy CI/CD integration (DevOps)
